note: Following: the deer walks or runs toward a goal, looking at it. The game calls this every frame while a deer follows.

this is part of: creature body

settings:
  walking speed: 60 cm per second
  running speed: 170 cm per second
  sharp turn speed: 30 cm per second
  acceleration: 40 cm per second squared
  stop distance: 300 cm
  turn gain: 2 degrees per second for each degree off course
  turn per speed: 2 degrees per second for each cm per second
  turn limit: 25 degrees per second
  sharp turn angle: 45 degrees
  sharp turn limit: 30 degrees per second
  running turn limit: 8 degrees per second
  turn slew: 20 degrees per second squared
  look limit: 30 degrees
  note: shortcut: the flying trot holds to about 188 cm/s, turning only 8 degrees per second at full speed; faster and sharper needs a gallop controller.

to steer toward, given goal (a place) and running (yes or no):
  set wandering to no
  note: Speed must not build up while down, and a turn started before the legs have taken the weight back topples it again.
  if fallen or time since standing up is less than settle time: stop

  set gap to flat (goal minus centre of mass)
  set turn needed to angle from heading to direction of gap
  note: Snapping the head far round swings enough mass to topple it.
  set head turn to clamp (angle from body facing to direction of gap) between -look limit and look limit

  note: Sharp turns are only stable at a slow trot.
  set sharp to size of turn needed is more than sharp turn angle
  note: Turning on the spot topples it, so the turn allowed grows with speed.
  if walk speed is at least run speed:
    set top turn to running turn limit
  otherwise if sharp:
    set top turn to sharp turn limit
  otherwise:
    set top turn to turn limit
  set top turn to smaller of walk speed times turn per speed and top turn
  note: A turn rate stepped in at once (follow start, sharp goal) topples it.
  set wanted turn to clamp (turn needed times turn gain) between -top turn and top turn
  move turn rate toward wanted turn by at most turn slew times frame time

  if sharp:
    set cruise to sharp turn speed
  otherwise if running:
    set cruise to running speed
  otherwise:
    set cruise to walking speed
  note: Brakes early enough to stop at the stop distance.
  set distance left to larger of 0 and (size of gap) minus stop distance
  set braking speed to square root of 2 times acceleration times distance left
  move walk speed toward smaller of cruise and braking speed by at most acceleration times frame time
